            <ArticleTitle>(+/-)8-Amino-5,6,7,8-tetrahydroisoquinolines as novel antinociceptive agents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3651-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Several amine-substituted 8-amino-5,6,7,8-tetrahydroisoquinolines were examined as conformationally-constrained analogs of the nicotinic cholinergic (nACh) 3-(aminomethyl)pyridines. Although these ligands failed to bind at nACh receptors, the N-ethyl-N-methyl analog 3d was found to be at least equipotent with nicotine in rodent tests of antinociception. The mechanism of action of 3d is currently unknown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
